    "q-105400": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 26",
      "problem": "Let $V=C[-1,1],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-1,1]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$ \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)={t}^{2},\\,g(t)=15t+3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}$ equals $15t.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=15t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}g(t){f}_{2}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(15t+3)\\cdot {t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}15{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{15}{4}{t}^{4}+{t}^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{15}{4}+1)-(\\frac{15}{4}-1) \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{f}_{2}(t){f}_{2}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{2}\\cdot {t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{5}{t}^{5}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-(-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{2}{(\\frac{2}{5})}\\cdot {t}^{2}=5{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =15t+5{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
