    "q-334241": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 28",
      "problem": "For which of the following values is the implicit Euler method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n\n- $\\lambda Δx=0.1$\n- $\\lambda Δx=0.8$\n- $\\lambda Δx=1.2$\n- $\\lambda Δx=5$\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the implicit Euler method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A numerical method \n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the implicit Euler method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the implicit Euler Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.1)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.1}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.1}| \\\\  & =0.9090…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.8)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.8}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.8}| \\\\  & =0.5555…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.2)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+1.2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{2.2}| \\\\  & =0.4545…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(5)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+5}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{6}| \\\\  & =0.1666…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV\".\n\nNote that, since the implicit Euler method is absolutely stable, it is stable for all possible values of $\\lambda Δx.$",
